      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For either endpoint punctured disk $P$, choose pairwise disjoint arcs from the $r$ inner boundary circles to the outer boundary and cut along them. Such a finite cut system exists by triangulating the compact planar surface and taking a spanning tree in its finite dual graph. The cut surface is a disk; reversing the cuts exhibits a graph spine with one cycle around each inner boundary. Thus $P$ deformation retracts to a wedge of $r$ circles, and [F5] identifies its fundamental group as free on the based positive boundary loops.",
