        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "For each endpoint, map the pair $(D^2,P)$ into $(B,X_\\tau)$ using the endpoint disk and its product tube. Naturality of the connecting map in [F2] sends the relative class of the $i$th endpoint disk to the relative cross-sectional disk class of the $i$th tube. By step 2.2 those classes map to the ordered basis of $H_1(X_\\tau)$. By step 1.2 their boundaries are the positive meridian basis of $H_1(P_\\pm)$. Each end inclusion therefore induces the asserted $H_1$ isomorphism. Since $H_2(P_\\pm)=H_2(X_\\tau)=0$, it also induces the asserted $H_2$ epimorphism.",
