      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The height condition says that the link meets the level sphere $\\Sigma$ exactly at the $n$ underpassing points. Hence $A_L\\cup B_L=X$ and $A_L\\cap B_L=\\Sigma_L$. The one-point compactification of the plane $\\mathbb R^2\\times\\{-1\\}$ is a sphere, so removing those $n$ points gives the stated punctured sphere. A sphere minus a finite nonempty set is path connected, and the half-space pieces remain path connected after removing finitely many one-dimensional arcs: a path between two points can be perturbed in finitely many coordinate balls to avoid those arcs, since a one-dimensional arc has codimension two in a three-manifold.",
          "step": "1.1",
