        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Every point of $B_L$ lies below height $-1$. For $0\\leq t<1$, move $(x,y,z)$ vertically to $(x,y,z-t/(1-t))$, and send $\\infty$ to itself; at $t=1$ send every point to $\\infty$. This is continuous in the one-point compactification, avoids $L_D$ because the link lies in $z\\geq-1$, and contracts $B_L$ to $\\infty$.",
          "step": "2.1",
