        {
          "id": "step-2-2",
          "claim": "Choose based small circles $c_1,\\ldots,c_n$ around the punctures. Attaching disks to the punctured sphere along all these circles gives $S^2$; [F3] therefore says their images normally generate $\\pi_1(\\Sigma_L)$. If $c_j$ is omitted, attaching disks along the other $n-1$ circles gives $S^2$ with only the $j$th point removed, which is homeomorphic to $\\mathbb R^2$ and is simply connected. The same van Kampen quotient argument shows the other $n-1$ circles normally generate.",
