          "claim": "Put $U=M\\setminus S$ and $V=N\\cup T$. These are path-connected open sets covering $M$. Their intersection consists of $N_-$, $N_+$, and the tube joining their end balls. Cover the intersection by the two side components with the respective half of the tube. Each set is path-connected and simply connected, and their overlap is a contractible middle tube. Hence [F1] gives $\\pi_1(U\\cap V)=1$.",
