          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Every group $G$ has a connected CW model $K(G,1)$. For every abelian group $A$ and every $n\\geq2$, there is a connected CW model $K(A,n)$. If two models carry identifications with the same group, they are homotopy equivalent by maps inducing the prescribed identification (with the usual basepoint transport in degree one).",
          "uses": [
