        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Construct $B\\phi$ on the one-skeleton of $BG$ by sending each based loop representing $g\\in G$ to a based loop representing $\\phi(g)\\in H$. Every two-cell attaching loop represents the identity in $G$, so its image represents the identity in $H$ and extends over the two-cell. For a cell of dimension $k\\geq3$, the attaching map is a sphere map into $BH$ and extends over the disk because $\\pi_{k-1}(BH)=0$ by [F1]. AC chooses the extensions over the set of cells. This gives a based map inducing $\\phi$.",
