          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "The maps $B\\phi\\circ c_X$ and $c_Y\\circ f$ induce the same homomorphism $\\phi$ on fundamental groups. On the vertices choose based paths joining their values, and on each one-cell fill the resulting boundary loop; that loop is null because the two induced fundamental-group maps agree. Inductively, the obstruction to extending the homotopy across each $k$-cell is a map $S^k\\to BH$, and it is null for $k\\geq2$ by [F1]. AC supplies the cell extensions. Hence the maps are based homotopic.",
