          "source": "lem-classifying-maps-are-natural-under-group-homomorphisms",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $f:(X,x_0)\\to(Y,y_0)$ be a based map of path-connected CW\ncomplexes, let $G=\\pi_1(X,x_0)$ and $H=\\pi_1(Y,y_0)$, and put\n$\\phi=f_*:G\\to H$. Let $c_X:X\\to BG$ and $c_Y:Y\\to BH$ be based classifying\nmaps inducing the identity on the identified fundamental groups. There is a\nbased map $B\\phi:BG\\to BH$ inducing $\\phi$, and\n$$\nB\\phi\\circ c_X\\simeq c_Y\\circ f\n$$\nby a based homotopy. Consequently the induced maps on singular homology commute.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-stallings-integral-lower-central-isomorphism",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $\\phi:A\\to B$ be a group homomorphism inducing an isomorphism\n$H_1(A;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_1(B;\\mathbb Z)$ and an epimorphism\n$H_2(A;\\mathbb Z)\\to H_2(B;\\mathbb Z)$. For a group $X$, define\n$\\Gamma_1X=X$ and $\\Gamma_{n+1}X=[X,\\Gamma_nX]$. Then for every finite\n$n\\ge1$, the induced homomorphism\n$$\nA/\\Gamma_nA\\longrightarrow B/\\Gamma_nB\n$$\nis an isomorphism.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
