          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Use integral homology. Let $L=K_1\\cup\\cdots\\cup K_r$ be a nonempty labeled oriented smooth link in $S^3$ with chosen pairwise disjoint product tubes and exterior $E_L$. Then $H_1(E_L;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z^r$, with the positive meridians as its ordered basis. Each boundary torus $T_i$ has a product basis consisting of its positive meridian and a degree-one section. There is a unique degree-one class on $T_i$ whose image has zero $i$th meridian coordinate; this class is primitive and has a simple closed representative.\n\nLet $\\tau$ be an $r$-component string link with chosen disjoint product tubes in $D^2\\times[0,1]$, exterior $X_\\tau$, and bottom and top punctured disks $P_-$ and $P_+$. Then each $\\pi_1(P_\\pm)$ is free on the positive endpoint meridians, $H_1(P_\\pm;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z^r$, and $H_2(P_\\pm;\\mathbb Z)=0$. The exterior satisfies $H_1(X_\\tau;\\mathbb Z)\\cong\\mathbb Z^r$ and $H_2(X_\\tau;\\mathbb Z)=0$. Each end inclusion sends its ordered positive meridian basis to the ordered positive meridian basis of $H_1(X_\\tau;\\mathbb Z)$. Consequently both induced homomorphisms on $H_1$ are isomorphisms and both induced homomorphisms on $H_2$ are surjective.",
