          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $A_L^\\circ=((\\mathbb R^2\\times(-1,\\infty))\\cup\\{\\infty\\})\\setminus L_D$.\nBy [F1], $\\pi_1(A_L^\\circ)\\cong\\pi_1(A_L)$. A small neighborhood $H$ of\n$\\infty$ in $A_L^\\circ$ is a half-ball disjoint from $L_D$. The open cover\n$A_L^\\circ=M\\cup H$ has intersection $H\\setminus\\{\\infty\\}$, which is\nhomeomorphic to $(0,1)\\times S^2_+$ and is contractible because the closed\nhemisphere $S^2_+$ is a disk. Since $H$ is also contractible, [F2] gives\n$\\pi_1(M)\\cong\\pi_1(A_L^\\circ)$.",
