          "claim": "Each $D_j$ is the image of the open region\n$(s,t)\\mapsto(\\gamma(s),-1+t(\\eta(s)+1))$ with $s\\in I_j$ and $0<t<1$;\nthis is an embedded open disk. At a projected double point, the underpassing\nbranch has height $-1$ and is absent from $M$, while the overpassing branch\nhas height greater than $-1$. Thus sheets over distinct intervals are disjoint.\nEach sheet is closed in $M$: its only limit points outside itself lie on the\nexcluded plane $z=-1$ or on the excluded link. Hence it is a proper smooth\nembedded simply connected surface.",
