          "quote": "Assume AC. Let $\\tau_B$ be the based 3-string link represented from bottom to\ntop by the pure braid word\n$$\n\\beta=(\\sigma_2^{-1}\\sigma_1)^3\n=\\sigma_2^{-1}\\sigma_1\\sigma_2^{-1}\\sigma_1\\sigma_2^{-1}\\sigma_1,\n$$\nwhere $\\sigma_i$ is the positive geometric half twist of adjacent strands in\nthe crossing convention for this library, and labels $1,2,3$ are assigned from\nleft to right at the bottom. Close each top endpoint to the corresponding\nbottom endpoint outside the braid cylinder; this is the mirror convention for\nthe standard Borromean link closure. Use the bottom meridians and the\ndiagram-induced blackboard product-tube parallels for this based braid. The\nthird string-link longitude and the matching based\nlongitude of its closed link have truncated expansion\n$$\nE(\\lambda_3)=1+X_1X_2-X_2X_1\\pmod{\\mathfrak m^3},\n$$\nso $\\mu_{\\tau_B}(1,2,3)=1$. Every pairwise linking number of the closed braid\nis zero, and its based closed-link residue candidate is\n$\\bar\\mu^b_{\\widehat{\\tau}_B}(1,2,3)=1$.\n\n~~~tikz\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85,>=stealth]\n  % Six adjacent half-twists, read from bottom to top.\n  % sigma_2^{-1}\n  \\draw[gray] (0,6) -- (0,5);\n  \\draw[thick,->] (1,6) .. controls (1.25,5.75) and (1.75,5.25) .. (2,5);\n  \\draw[thick,dashed,->] (2,6) .. controls (1.75,5.75) and (1.25,5.25) .. (1,5);\n  \\node at (0.55,5.5) {$\\sigma_2^{-1}$};\n  % sigma_1\n  \\draw[thick,dashed,->] (0,5) .. controls (0.25,4.75) and (0.75,4.25) .. (1,4);\n  \\draw[thick,->] (1,5) .. controls (0.75,4.75) and (0.25,4.25) .. (0,4);\n  \\draw[gray] (2,5) -- (2,4);\n  \\node at (1.45,4.5) {$\\sigma_1$};\n  % sigma_2^{-1}\n  \\draw[gray] (0,4) -- (0,3);\n  \\draw[thick,->] (1,4) .. controls (1.25,3.75) and (1.75,3.25) .. (2,3);\n  \\draw[thick,dashed,->] (2,4) .. controls (1.75,3.75) and (1.25,3.25) .. (1,3);\n  \\node at (0.55,3.5) {$\\sigma_2^{-1}$};\n  % sigma_1\n  \\draw[thick,dashed,->] (0,3) .. controls (0.25,2.75) and (0.75,2.